# The init a product runs when its product.env says INIT=systemd, or nothing: mica-systemd wires the floor's
# lifecycle tools into systemd (units, mounts, networkd, resolved, timesyncd, journald in RAM) and grows DATA with
# systemd-repart; the rest are the upstream roots of the Base lock it depends on
# (mica-system-base:docs/floor-and-options.md, "The init").
mica-systemd
systemd
systemd-sysv
udev
systemd-resolved
systemd-timesyncd
systemd-repart
